      {
        "alt": "Three aligned forest-plot panels show ratios and participant-cluster-robust 95% confidence intervals for free versus work day, active versus sedentary day status, and each additional hour of previous sleep. Rows compare the primary near-eye estimate with complementary chest, paired-day near-eye and chest, and gap-timing-unaware near-eye and chest estimates. Activity ratios remain above the null ratio of one across the displayed analyses, whereas previous-sleep intervals include one.",
        "caption": "Figure 1: Estimated mean hourly melEDI among observed hours that met the support criteria. Points and bars are ratios and participant-cluster-robust 95% CIs; the dashed line is the null ratio of 1. Near-eye is the primary sensor position, and chest estimates are complementary non-ocular comparisons.",
