      {
        "alt": "Three vertically aligned panels summarize exploratory near-eye melEDI by day type and local clock time. The top panel overlays work-day and free-day expected curves with pointwise 95% bands and dots at integer hours supported in all nine sites. The middle panel shows free day divided by work day with a dashed null line at ratio one; integer-hour points are filled when the pointwise interval excludes one and hollow when it includes one. The bottom panel shows available participant-hours for each day type at every integer hour.",
        "caption": "Figure 5: Exploratory nonlinear day-type timing display: overlaid estimated curves, the complete response-scale free-day/work-day contrast, and participant-hour support. The other binary factor and all nine sites receive equal weight. A pointwise 95% CI applies at one displayed hour, not to the whole curve. Filled and hollow points distinguish intervals that exclude and include the null ratio of 1; this is not a multiplicity-controlled or simultaneous whole-curve test.",
